{{Quote|And if they find out he's dead because of you, you're gonna wish you never left Alderaan. I saw the tear.|Imperial shuttle pilot, to Cara Dune|<ref name="Chapter 16">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 16: The Rescue}}</ref>}}
[[File:CaraDune-SWI194.png|thumb|right|250px|Rebel and New Republic Shock Trooper Cara Dune wore a tear beneath her left eye.]]
A '''tear''' was a small [[tattoo]] of the [[Rebel Alliance starbird|Rebel Alliance Starbird]] situated below the left eye of the wearer. The motif was worn as a symbol of solidarity among survivors of the destruction of [[Alderaan]]. It was common enough among [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel]] fighters from the doomed planet that it was recognizable even among [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] troops. When ex-Rebel and [[New Republic]] [[Shock trooper|dropper]] [[Carasynthia Dune|Cara Dune]] helped hijack a [[Lambda-class T-4a shuttle|''Lambda''-class shuttle]] from [[Gideon|Moff Gideon's]] [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|remnant forces]]<ref name="Chapter 16" /> in [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> the copilot immediately recognized her as an [[Alderaanian]] from her tear.<ref name="Chapter 16" />

{{Stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The tear is one of several tattoos applied to actress [[Gina Carano]] for her role as Cara Dune in the [[Disney+]] series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]''. While the bars on her bicep were revealed in the first season episode "[[Chapter 7: The Reckoning|The Reckoning]]" to identify her as a Rebel and New Republic Shock Trooper, the meaning of the tear was not mentioned until [[Chapter 16: The Rescue|the second season finale]].<ref name="CBR">{{WebCite|url=https://www.cbr.com/the-mandalorian-meaning-cara-dune-eye-tattoo|text=The Mandalorian Reveals the Tragic Meaning of Cara Dune's Eye Tattoo|author=Bloom, Mike|date=2020-12-19|work=[https://www.cbr.com CBR.com]|archivedate=20201220130054}}</ref>

Teardrop tattoos are worn in real life, though may have a variety of meanings. They are often associated with prison culture, but are also worn to signify sorrow or loss.<ref name="Dictionary">{{WebCite|url=https://www.dictionary.com/e/pop-culture/teardrop-tattoo|text=teardrop tattoo|work=[https://www.dictionary.com Dictionary.com]|archivedate=20201112020317}}</ref>

